<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cervera</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cervera is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> in Catalonia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-courts">Catalan Courts</a> met there several times, and in 1717 Philip V closed the other Catalan universities and founded a single university at Cervera, which lasted until it moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> in 1842.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cervera.jpg" alt="Cervera" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alberto-g-rovi · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panoramica_de_Cervera_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
